== (i) validity: analytic margin + exhaustive scan ==
  analytic run margin v3(1-kappa) - A(1+kappa) = 0.3165 > 0   (Lemma W: validity at ALL orders)
  stationary state omega = [0.036477 0.021028 0.942495]   (min component 0.0210 >= 0)
  exhaustive scan, all 2^16 words to length 16: min p(w) = 7.333e-06  (>= 0)
  -> the clock is a VALID stationary process, proven analytically
     and scanned exhaustively.

== (ii) the record (Hankel) rank is exactly 3 ==
  Hankel (63x63) singular values: 1.9705, 0.0433, 0.0142, then 4.6e-16
  -> rank 3: the process has a FINITE record dimension.

== (iii) p(1^n)/kappa^n = a + b cos(n theta + c), exactly ==
  fit residual = 3.33e-16   a = 0.942495   |b| = 0.059545  (b != 0)
  best periodicity over P <= 12: min_P max_n |p_n - p_(n+P)| = 0.0168  (bounded away from 0)
  -> the normalized diagonal sequence oscillates at theta = 1 rad
     (theta/2pi irrational) ON the decay circle and fits NO
     rational period: exactly the structure Theorem B forbids for
     finite positive realizations.

== (iv) reversibility ==
  max |p(w) - p(reverse w)| over all words to length 12 = 8.33e-17
  -> the clock is REVERSIBLE (stationary renewal: iid blocks):
     the separation lands INSIDE the corpus' eventless-compatible
     class.

== (v) RP status: reversible but NOT reflection-positive ==
  reflection Gram on words to length 4 (31x31): min eigenvalue = -4.137e-02  (FAILS PSD)
  diagonal Hankel [p(1^(i+j))] 8x8: min eigenvalue = -9.958e-03  (FAILS the moment test)
  -> the clock is reversible yet NOT RP - and P8's typed theorem
     says it CANNOT be: site-RP forces the diagonal to be a
     Hamburger moment sequence (real spectrum); oscillation on
     the decay circle requires complex eigenvalues kappa e^(+-i),
     which the failed Hankel PSD test detects.  Consistency note:
     reversibility does NOT imply RP without a Markov
     presentation - exactly P10 T4's hypothesis, here sharp.
  THE SEPARATION (Theorem B + this witness):
       { finite record laws }  STRICTLY INSIDE
       { reversible, valid, finite-record-rank processes }.
  THE RESIDUE (named (PR-RP)): whether RP + finite rank implies
     a finite record law - the clock mechanism is EXCLUDED from
     that class by the moment theorem, so the separation witness
     must be different there if it exists at all (Anderson's
     positive-realization theorem suggests strictly-dominant RP
     processes are realizable, possibly at higher dimension).
== p16a done ==
